    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d218">

                <pb facs="0283" n="213" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv01/pg213"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">841.731/2103: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Special Representative</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >House</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-28T12:00:00+00:00"
                            >November 28, 1918—12 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 28—9:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>195. Secret for the President. Referring to our 137 and 146.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d218-f1"/> I am advised through Wiseman that the British Government have <pb facs="0284" n="214"
                        xml:id="pg214"/> abolished the political censorship of press despatches for
                    the United States from Great Britain.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edward House</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
